From 8e1239421bfeb5d4eb84cb29c700592bcb71e595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 18:19:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0228 -- DOS default gameport axis->action mappings
 (Phase 3 / #40)

Re-engage (P3-rework): the in-game flightstick could not MOVE the player
(buttons worked). Root cause: the DOS default mapping table leaves
jaxis=-1 for every action (input_init), and the no-saved-settings branch
never calls input_set_mappings, so input_get_action_axis() never matched
and the engine's in-game axis loop had nothing bound. BIND_* (patch
0227) only parses k:/b:, never an axis -- so no path set a default axis.

Fix: add DOS-only (__DJGPP__) default gameport axis->action mappings in
input_init -- axis 0 (X) -/+ = LEFT/RIGHT, axis 1 (Y) -/+ = UP/DOWN on
the 4 directional actions. input_get_action_axis() consults only the
SIGN of jaxis_value, so +/-1 suffices; the existing in-game axis loop
(SDL_GetJoystickAxis past the 20000 deadzone) is already correct and now
has bindings. Scope: DEFAULT directional mappings only -- axis remapping
is intentionally NOT exposed this round.

Pairs with p3-sdl's CalibrateAxis per-side scaling fix (so an
offset-center flightstick reaches full range past the 20000 deadzone);
the engine reads SDL_GetJoystickAxis so the SDL read-method is
transparent to this mapping.

Caveat: an EXISTING settings.dat from before this patch carries jaxis=-1
and input_set_mappings overwrites these defaults on load; a fresh run
(no settings.dat) applies them and settings_save then persists them.

Workspace-local; never upstreamed. GPLv3 (derivative of NXEngine-evo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input.cpp | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input.cpp b/src/input.cpp
index 8e6a05c..42aac1c 100644
--- a/src/input.cpp
+++ b/src/input.cpp
@@ -89,6 +89,30 @@ bool input_init(void)
   mappings[ESCKEY].jbut       = 11; // -
 #endif
 
+#if defined(__DJGPP__)
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0228, Phase 3 / #40): default gameport axis->action
+  // mappings so an analog stick / flightstick moves the player out of the box.
+  // The base DOS default table leaves jaxis=-1 for every action, and the
+  // no-saved-settings branch (settings.cpp) never calls input_set_mappings, so
+  // without these defaults input_get_action_axis() never matches and the stick
+  // is DEAD in-game (buttons still work via jbut). The SDL3-DOS gameport
+  // reports 2 axes: axis 0 = X (left/right), axis 1 = Y (up/down); resting
+  // negative = left / up. input_get_action_axis() consults only the SIGN of
+  // jaxis_value, so +/-1 is sufficient. Directional actions only -- axis
+  // remapping is not exposed this round (BIND_* grammar stays k:/b:).
+  // NOTE: an EXISTING settings.dat from before this patch carries jaxis=-1 and
+  // input_set_mappings will overwrite these defaults on load; a fresh run (no
+  // settings.dat) applies them and settings_save then persists them.
+  mappings[LEFTKEY].jaxis        = 0;
+  mappings[LEFTKEY].jaxis_value  = -1;
+  mappings[RIGHTKEY].jaxis       = 0;
+  mappings[RIGHTKEY].jaxis_value = 1;
+  mappings[UPKEY].jaxis          = 1;
+  mappings[UPKEY].jaxis_value    = -1;
+  mappings[DOWNKEY].jaxis        = 1;
+  mappings[DOWNKEY].jaxis_value  = 1;
+#endif
+
   mappings[F1KEY].key  = SDLK_F1;
   mappings[F2KEY].key  = SDLK_F2;
   mappings[F3KEY].key  = SDLK_F3;
